cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite **both** powelleem and the NEEMP
  paper (see `references` below) — powelleem's parameter-fitting protocol
  is directly inspired by NEEMP.
type: software
title: 'powelleem: EEM parameter fitting with analytical Jacobian and Powell solvers'
version: 0.1.0a0
date-released: '2026-05-22'
authors:
  - family-names: Godin
    given-names: Guillaume
license: MIT
url: 'https://github.com/guillaume-godin/powelleem'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/guillaume-godin/powelleem'
abstract: >-
  A modern Python implementation of the Electronegativity Equalization Method
  parameter fitting pipeline, with an analytical Jacobian (via the implicit
  function theorem), six interchangeable solvers (NumPy + LM, NEWUOA, BOBYQA,
  JAX + Adam, JAX + LM, and a DE/NEWUOA hybrid that reproduces the original
  MATLAB DE_UOA_FINAL pipeline), and a statistical benchmark harness. The
  parameter-fitting protocol — atom typing, default-parameter fallback
  hierarchy, hybrid global/local optimisation, validation suite — is directly
  inspired by NEEMP (Raček et al., J. Cheminform. 2016, 8, 57).
keywords:
  - EEM
  - electronegativity equalization
  - NEEMP
  - partial charges
  - NEWUOA
  - BOBYQA
  - Levenberg-Marquardt
  - molecular descriptors
  - RDKit
  - MMFF94
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      NEEMP: software for validation, accurate calculation and fast
      parameterization of EEM charges
    authors:
